{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"byplw7tn0","tool_use_id":"toolu_01E8NUGcsdYJqvHoH9qNxU5V","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"cd \"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-272-230f\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nWI-272: disposition of 009-CRITIQUE U5 — status fidelity complete, palette uniformity is a new owner WI\n\nWI-272 (dashboard work-item status fidelity, M-2) is built and Review-A\nAPPROVED (008). The build (a6abfb8 + c67e85b) preserves the full six-state\nlifecycle — queued|active|done|deferred|blocked|retired — across every When-tab\nrender surface: STATUS_FILL/CSS vars, A3 glyphs (deferred ▽, blocked ◼), the\nlegend, the detail badge emitted straight from STATUS_FILL ($status_color), and\nthe flat-DAG fallback routed through the single _wi_st helper. The new fills\n#6b21a8/#b91c1c are byte-distinct from every other palette and clear WCAG AA.\n\nThe sole outstanding critique finding, U5 (009-CRITIQUE), is OUT OF SCOPE for\nWI-272 and is handed to @owner as a new dashboard-palette-uniformity WI. U5's\ncollisions (done #047857 == Test Case type; active #b45309 == Process Guide\ntype; phase accents share type hue families) are PRE-EXISTING and systemic —\nWI-272 touched none of TIER_FILL/OKF_TYPE_FILL/PHASE_ACCENTS and introduced no\nbyte-identical collision. U5's remedy is a cross-tab palette-token refactor\nreassigning established semantic type colours, which is a design decision (the\nfinding is routed to @owner) and would itself require a fresh render critique.\nPer the repo pattern (M-2 -> WI-272, M-3 -> WI-273) and render-dashboard-critique\n(\"file findings as their own WIs\"), U5 becomes its own WI, not scope creep here.\n\nNo code change this session. Full rationale + verification evidence in\ndocs/reviews/1-g3-WI-272-230f/010-BUILD-DISPOSITION-c67e85b.md.\n\nVerification (main-repo .venv, Python 3.11.9):\n- gen_trajectory.py --root . --check -> project-state dashboard up to date.\n- targeted fidelity tests: 6 passed.\n- check_trajectory --strict: only render red is the by-design perceptual-stale\n  gate (clears via post-integration critique); remaining reds are WI-275\n  root-coordination-truth the integrator scrubs.\n\nWI: WI-272\nTrain: 1-g3-WI-272-230f\nBase: 747f1529c20688e726d76282160b0f9702d5c738\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log -1 --format=\"%H %s\" && echo \"=== trailers ===\" && git log -1 --format=\"%(trailers:key=WI)%(trailers:key=Train)%(trailers:key=Base)\"","uuid":"f96079fe-5159-43ec-8238-528e7550c829","session_id":"b3fe8054-9261-4e59-a2db-dbfda6ef04ea"}
